#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:31
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Help Index</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:33
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the time of writing, for most installations of &kde; the entire search "
"engine function in &khelpcenter; is disabled, and settings made in this "
"&kcontrol; module will have no effect. We hope to have it back in a future "
"release."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:35
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kde; comes with a lot of documentation for applications and components. "
"While it is possible to just browse the manuals until you find that piece of "
"information you're looking for, this may be a very time-consuming task. To "
"make this easier for you, &kde; offers fulltext search using a program "
"called <application>ht://dig</application>. It works quite similar to search "
"engines on the web, in fact some search engines you know might even use it. "
"Just click on the <guilabel>Search</guilabel> tab in the &khelpcenter;, "
"enter the word you are looking for, click <guibutton>Search</guibutton> and "
"enjoy!"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:46
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"However, to make use of this feature, <application>ht://dig</application> "
"has to be installed on your system and &kde; has to be configured to make "
"use of it. This control module tries to help you doing the latter. If you "
"haven't installed <application>ht://dig</application> and it wasn't shipped "
"with your operating system you have to get ht://dig yourself. Have a look at "
"<ulink url=\"http://www.htdig.org\">the ht://dig homepage</ulink> on how to "
"download and install it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:55
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you first start, you are in display mode only. To modify your settings, "
"click on <guibutton>Administrator Mode</guibutton>. If you are logged in as "
"<systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, you will go straight to "
"the change dialog. If not, &kde; will ask for a superuser password."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Use</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two important things to tell &kde; so it can make use of the "
"fulltext search engine:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"where to find the <application>ht://dig</application> programs KDE uses for "
"fulltext search"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "where to search"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <application>ht://dig</application> Programs"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are three programs &kde; needs that come with <application>ht://dig</"
"application>: <command>htdig</command>, <command>htsearch</command> and "
"<command>htmerge</command>. For each program you have to provide the full "
"path including the program name, for example: <filename class=\"directory\">/"
"usr/bin/htdig</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Where exactly these programs are installed depends on your operating system "
"or your distribution. However, there are some good guesses you might want to "
"try:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>htdig</command> and <command>htmerge</command> are often found in "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr/bin/</filename> or in something like "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr/local/www/htdig/bin/</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"the <command>htsearch</command> command is often found in a sub folder "
"called <filename class=\"directory\">cgi-bin</filename>, for example "
"<filename class=\"directory\">/usr/local/httpd/cgi-bin/</filename>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To find out where for example <command>htdig</command> is installed you can "
"always type <command>whereis htdig</command> on the console. "
"<command>whereis</command> will look for the specified command in the "
"standard execution path folders. However, folders like <filename class="
"\"directory\">cgi-bin</filename> are often not in the standard execution "
"path."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "Scope and Search Paths"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:113
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this section you can choose which help resources should be indexed, &ie; "
"made available to the search engine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Scope</guilabel> frame you can select some typical "
"resources you want to be indexed, &ie; the &kde; help files, and the "
"information offered by the <command>man</command> and <command>info</"
"command> commands. Note that some of those may still be disabled, which "
"means that support for them has not been added yet."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Maybe you have additional files you want to access using the &khelpcenter; "
"fulltext search feature. For example, you might have an <acronym>HTML</"
"acronym> reference installed in <filename>/home/jdoe/docs/selfhtml</"
"filename>. By adding this path to the list of additional search paths you "
"make this documentation available to &khelpcenter;'s fulltext search, too. "
"Just click on the <guibutton>Add</guibutton> button and a file dialog will "
"ask you for an additional search folder. Select <filename class=\"directory"
"\">/home/jdoe/docs/selfhtml</filename> and click <guibutton>OK</guibutton>. "
"To remove an additional search path, just select it and click "
"<guibutton>Delete</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:135
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Your changes to the scope and additional search paths will not take effect "
"if you don't click on the <guibutton>Generate index</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""
